WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.093
How could we move that heavy boat?

2
00:00:04.094 --> 00:00:07.344
I stood on the deck, looking at the wreckage around us.

3
00:00:07.345 --> 00:00:09.861
"We need a lever and rollers!" I cried.

4
00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:12.599
"Fetch me a sturdy wooden plank for a lever.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.654
We can make rollers from what's left of a mast."

6
00:00:18.655 --> 00:00:22.772
Fritz quickly brought a plank, and I cut up a mast.

7
00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:27.914
Then I raised the bow of our boat with the plank while my sons placed a roller under it.

8
00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:34.456
We repeated the process, placing two more rollers under the boat.

9
00:00:34.457 --> 00:00:42.072
When we once again began to push, we were able to launch our boat into the water.

10
00:00:42.073 --> 00:00:46.523
"Now, my beloved family," I announced, "it's time to make our escape.

11
00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:49.119
Leave plenty of food near the animals.

12
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.054
Then collect everything that may be of use to us."

13
00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:54.779
The boys joyfully obeyed me.

14
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.473
From the large quantity of things they gathered, I chose canvas for a tent,

15
00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:07.901
a chest of carpenter's tools, fishing rods, an iron pot, cases of biscuits and dried soup, and some other items.

16
00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:12.006
We now began to take our seats, each one of us in our own tub.

17
00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:16.414
Just then we heard the roosters crowing as if scolding us for abandoning them.

18
00:01:16.415 --> 00:01:21.924
"Let's take them with us," urged my wife.

19
00:01:21.925 --> 00:01:30.709
So we placed ten hens and a couple of roosters in one tub with some wire netting over the top.

20
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:38.375
The ducks and geese took to the water at once while the pigeons swiftly flew toward shore.

21
00:01:38.376 --> 00:01:44.387
"This is my contribution," said my wife, throwing a mysterious bag to Franz.

22
00:01:44.388 --> 00:01:51.750
All being ready, we cast off and moved away from the wreck.

23
00:01:51.751 --> 00:01:55.108
My good, brave wife sat in the first compartment.

24
00:01:55.109 --> 00:02:00.039
Then came Franz, our youngest son, followed by Fritz, our oldest son.

25
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.130
The center tubs contained our valuable cargo.

26
00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:10.032
Then came our third son, bold Jack, followed by Ernest, our intelligent but rather lazy second son.

27
00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:14.980
I stood in the stern, trying to guide the boat to a safe landing place.

28
00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:19.257
We had left the two large dogs, Turk and Juno on the wreck.

29
00:02:19.258 --> 00:02:24.100
But when they saw us deserting them, they sprang into the sea after us.

30
00:02:24.101 --> 00:02:30.079
As we neared the shore, it appeared rocky and barren.

31
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:36.209
The geese and ducks, however, found an opening between the rocks where a stream flowed into the sea.

32
00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:45.747
I steered after them, and we soon found ourselves in a small, calm bay.

33
00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:51.200
As soon as we could gather our children around us on dry land, we knelt in prayer.

34
00:02:51.201 --> 00:02:54.858
Then together we unloaded the boat and set up a tent.

35
00:02:54.859 --> 00:02:58.704
The younger boys quickly gathered moss and grass for beds.

36
00:02:58.705 --> 00:03:03.050
I made a fireplace with some large flat stones near the brook.

37
00:03:03.051 --> 00:03:07.120
Then my wife began making soup with the help of little Franz.

38
00:03:07.121 --> 00:03:12.604
"Mama, don't you want some beef?" he asked as she added water to the dried soup.

39
00:03:12.605 --> 00:03:15.626
"Where can I get it, dear?" she reminded him.

40
00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:18.348
"We're a long way from a butcher's shop."

41
00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:20.889
"Oh," he said quietly.

42
00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:24.986
Meanwhile Fritz climbed over the rocks to see what lay beyond the stream.

43
00:03:24.987 --> 00:03:30.524
That kind of brisk exercise didn't suit Ernest, so he wandered down to the beach.

44
00:03:30.525 --> 00:03:34.490
Jack scrambled among the rocks searching for shellfish.

45
00:03:34.491 --> 00:03:38.137
I was eager to grab two casks that had been floating near our boat.

46
00:03:38.138 --> 00:03:41.594
While struggling to do that, I heard Jack cry out.

47
00:03:41.595 --> 00:03:44.605
"Help!" he screamed.

48
00:03:44.606 --> 00:03:49.906
Fearing he was in great danger, I ran and found him standing in a deep pool.

49
00:03:49.907 --> 00:03:53.758
A huge lobster had caught his leg in its powerful claw!

50
00:03:53.759 --> 00:03:55.902
Poor Jack was very frightened.

51
00:03:55.903 --> 00:03:59.269
"It won't let me go!" he cried.

52
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.884
I grabbed the lobster firmly by the back, and it released its grip.

53
00:04:02.885 --> 00:04:06.800
Jack carried the lobster triumphantly to the tent.

54
00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:12.031
He urged his mother to add it to the soup, but she decided to save it for another meal.

55
00:04:12.032 --> 00:04:16.574
"Congratulations, Jack," I said. "You're the first to discover something useful."

56
00:04:16.575 --> 00:04:24.400
"I found something good to eat too. Oysters!" said Ernest.

57
00:04:24.401 --> 00:04:26.806
"But I didn't want to get my feet wet.

58
00:04:26.807 --> 00:04:31.321
And I found sea salt in the crevices of the rocks."

59
00:04:31.322 --> 00:04:35.212
"Never let me hear you object to getting your feet wet," I said.

60
00:04:35.213 --> 00:04:39.499
"See how quickly the sun has dried Jack and me."

61
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.188
My wife stirred the soup with a stick.

62
00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:47.618
"Our soup is ready, but how will we eat it without bowls or spoons?"

63
00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:50.586
"Oyster shells!" Ernest exclaimed.

64
00:04:50.587 --> 00:04:57.274
The boys ran off to get some oysters.

65
00:04:57.275 --> 00:05:06.422
By the time they came back, Fritz had also returned with reports of the beautiful country that lay beyond the stream.

66
00:05:06.423 --> 00:05:12.497
We ate the oysters and scooped up our soup with the shells.

67
00:05:12.498 --> 00:05:19.457
As the sun set, my wife pulled some oats from her mysterious bag and fed the poultry.

68
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:26.479
Our first day ashore drew peacefully to a close.

